# grove — the repository's only ignore file (adr-0048 D4).
#
# Grove carried no .gitignore at all while it had no dependencies. It needs one
# now, and the reason is mechanical rather than tidiness: the guard derives its
# change set from `git status --porcelain -uall` (guard-core.mjs
# `deriveChangeSet`), which lists every untracked file individually. An
# unignored hoisted install would put thousands of third-party paths into the
# change set of every run in this repository.
#
# The install is hoisted to the root by the workspace declaration in
# package.json, but npm may still place a nested tree beside a workspace
# member, so the rule is depth-independent.
node_modules/
